  "experimental_conditions": {
    "001": {
      "0": {
        "detector": [
          {
            "x4_code": "(TELES,SI,IOCH)",
            "free_txt": [
              " The particle identification (PID) was",
              "performed by analyzing the cyclotron period of",
              "emitted light charged particles in a uniform magnetic",
              "field, combined with four sets of dE-E telescopes to",
              "detect 14C residues. The intensity of the incoming",
              "beam was monitored using a downstream ionization",
              "chamber."
            ]
          }
        ],
        "facility": [
          {
            "x4_code": "(LINAC,1USAANL)",
            "free_txt": [
              " ATLAS facility at the Argonne",
              "National Laboratory."
            ]
          }
        ],
        "method": [
          {
            "x4_code": "(EDE)",
            "free_txt": [
              " The kinematic reconstruction was achieved",
              "through high precision position-sensitive silicon",
              "detector arrays, which provided both position and",
              "energy information. This approach enabled the",
              "extraction of differential cross sections for",
              "transfer reactions populating the ground state (g.s.)",
              "of 14C, covering a range of center-of-mass angles",
              " (c.m.) from 15 to 35 degrees."
            ]
          }
        ],
        "rel-ref": [
          {
            "x4_code": "(R,C3086001,Y.Jiang+,J,AJ,989,231,2025)",
            "free_txt": [
              " 1H(15C,p) and",
              "2H(15C,t) data."
            ]
          }
        ],
        "sample": [
          {
            "x4_code": null,
            "free_txt": [
              "The 15C beam bombarded a target of deuterated",
              "polyethylene (CD2)n of thickness 363(20) microg/cm2",
              "or polyethylene (CH2)n of thickness 387(22)",
              "microg/cm2, which corresponded to the measurement of",
              "15C(p,d)14C and 15C(d,t)14C, respectively."
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "002": {
      "0": {
        "analysis": [
          {
            "x4_code": null,
            "free_txt": [
              "The spectroscopic factors (SF) and asymptotic",
              "normalization coefficient (ANC) of the 15Cg.s. were",
              "determined from angular distributions using the",
              "distorted-wave Born approximation (DWBA) theory. Two",
              "consistent SFs were derived from the (p,d) and (d,t)",
              "reactions, which were subsequently used to deduce the",
              "14C(n,gamma)15C reaction cross section and the",
              "corresponding stellar reaction rate."
            ]
          }
        ],
